# Code: a for-loop as things, properties, relations and change.
title "What a for-loop does"

group state part-of=[i,n] label="loop condition: i < n"
mark i     bar value=0 label="i"
mark n     bar value=4 label="n"
mark total bar sum=0   label="total"

Say: "i starts at zero and n is four. While i is shorter than n, we keep going."
focus total
Say: "Each pass adds i to the total, |a| then i grows by one."
@a morph i.value 0 -> 1 0.8s
Say: "Pass two. |b|"
@b morph total.sum 0 -> 1 0.8s
@b morph i.value 1 -> 2 0.8s
Say: "Pass three. |c|"
@c morph total.sum 1 -> 3 0.8s
@c morph i.value 2 -> 3 0.8s
Say: "Pass four. |d|"
@d morph total.sum 3 -> 6 0.8s
@d morph i.value 3 -> 4 0.8s
focus state
Say: "Now i equals n, the condition is false, and the loop stops with a total of six."
focus none
